**Emitter shape chosen** — member emission inside the group section, the upstream shape from `group-edge-graphviz.observed`:
- Member-bearing group: `( name\n  [ x ] { attrs }\n  [ y ]\n) { group attrs }` — header `( name` (same group-name escaping), each member's node declaration (attributes included) indented two spaces, then `)` and the group attribute block after it (matches upstream `( inner\n  [ a ]\n) { group: outer; }`).
- Empty groups keep the existing `( name ) { attrs }` form (no upstream evidence for empty sections; parser already reads it).
- Duplicate handling: member nodes are excluded from pass 2 (declaration_pass) and marked in the `declared` set so pass 4 never re-emits them as isolated bare nodes — exactly one declaration per member. `group_pass` now takes `&mut HashSet<usize>`.
- Parser untouched: a node line inside a group scope already joins that group (c6 rule in `parse/text/node.rs`), so the emitter's output round-trips with zero parser changes.

**Spec rows amended** — `specs/ge-txt_render.md` c3 and p3: group-membership carve-out dropped (cited gently-0kg→gently-8jf closure), group-endpoint-edge exclusion retained; mirror deployed via `tools/deploy_specs.py` in the same commit; spk-compiled props recompiled in `7c26cbe`.

